  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Amit Govind Vibhute vs The State Of Maharashtra on 3 April, 2023 Author: Anuja Prabhudessai Bench: Anuja Prabhudessai 6 aba 975-23.d In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 975 Of 2023 Amit Govind Vibhute ..Applicant v/s. The State of Maharashtra . ..Respondents Ms. Manisha Devkar for the Applicant. Mr. Shrikant Yadav, App for the State. Coram : Anuja Prabhudessai ,J. Dated : 3rd April, 2023. P.C. 1.",
    "facts": "It is alleged that the driver had disclosed that the said Gutkha was owned by the Applicant and was being transported at his instance. accused, prima facie, there is no other material to show the involvement of the Applicant in the crime. 2. This is an application for pre-arrest bail in connection with C.R. No. 106 of 2023 registered with Mangalvedha Police Station, Solapur for offence punishable under Sections 188, 272, 273 and 328 of IPC and under Sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(ii), 26(2)(iv), 3(1)(zz)(iv) and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. Applicant is accused No.3. 3. It is already recorded in the order dated 03.04.2023 that the concerned vehicle transporting Gutkha was intercepted and driver has named the Applicant. The Applicant is protected under order of this court since April 2023 for last more than 2 years. 94-ABA-975-2023 (CR).doc 4. Learned APP on instructions of the Officer of the concerned Police Station (who is present in the Court) submits that investigation is complete and chargesheet in respect of other accused is already Amit Govind Vibhute vs The State Of Maharashtra on 25 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/60779475/ 1 filed. However, the Applicant was shown as absconding. Considering that the Applicant was protected by order of this Court in anticipatory bail application, he could not have been shown as absconding.",
    "arguments": "5. Learned Counsel for the Applicant submits that the Applicant had already reported to the concerned Police Station on 18.07.2025 under earlier order of this court.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5. Learned Counsel for the Applicant submits that the Applicant had already reported to the concerned Police Station on 18.07.2025 under earlier order of this court.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
